================================================================
 IPA v2.6L — AP-local TX-stall recovery (rmnet watchdog harvest)
================================================================

 Incremental, opt-in patch. Apply ON TOP OF the 6.19 IPA port:

   patch -p1 < patches/sdm660-ipa-port-4.19-to-6.19.nosondy.patch
   patch -p1 < patches/ipa-tx-stall-recovery.patch          # <-- this

 Full rationale: patches/ipa-tx-stall-recovery.DESIGN.md

 WHAT IT DOES
   Turns the inert UL TX-stall watchdog into a real, bounded, AP-local
   recovery. Today ipa_wwan_tx_timeout() only logs "data stall in UL"
   (faithfully copied from vendor, which leans on SSR for recovery). On
   mainline q6v5 the SSR chain is unreliable and the port deliberately
   defanged the is_ssr path (re-registering the single ipa-driver.ko
   across SSR broke rmnet_ipa0 creation under insmod), so a lost SPS EOT
   can freeze uplink permanently until reboot.

 THE STALL (self-deadlock)
   A lost/coalesced SPS EOT on the egress pipe (APPS_LAN_WAN_PROD) means
   ipa_sps_irq_tx_notify() never runs -> completed descriptors are not
   harvested -> outstanding_pkts stays at the high watermark (64) ->
   ipa_wwan_xmit() calls netif_stop_queue() -> no new TX -> no new EOT ->
   the harvest is never re-armed. The netdev watchdog (watchdog_timeo =
   1000 ms) then fires ipa_wwan_tx_timeout().

 THE FIX
   ipa2_tx_dp_kick_stalled_pipe() (ipa_dp.c) replicates the SPS_EVENT_EOT
   branch of ipa_sps_irq_tx_notify() for the egress client: vote the IPA
   clock, switch the pipe to POLL mode, set curr_polling_state and queue
   sys->work -> ipa_handle_tx() -> sps_get_iovec() harvest -> each packet
   completion callback decrements outstanding_pkts and wakes the queue.
   outstanding_pkts drops NATURALLY, one per genuinely-completed
   descriptor -- no manual counter reset, so no underflow.

   ipa_wwan_tx_timeout() (rmnet_ipa.c) schedules the harvest out of timer
   context, tracks progress across ticks, logs "modem-side, not AP-
   recoverable" after IPA_TX_STALL_MODEM_THRESH no-progress kicks, and
   stops kicking after IPA_TX_STALL_GIVEUP (await SSR/reboot). A genuine
   completion clears the backoff.

 WHY IT IS SAFE
   sps_get_iovec() reads only the AP's own BAM pipe descriptor FIFO. It
   never touches modem-owned IPA state, so it cannot cross the XPU /
   TrustZone boundary (any AP poke at modem state hard-resets a fuse-blown
   retail device). The same action recovers a lost-EOT (AP-side) stall and
   is a harmless no-op for a modem-side one -- no detection needed.

 NON-GOALS
   - does not touch modem-owned state (XPU-safe)
   - does not reset/zero outstanding_pkts (no underflow)
   - does not (un)register the driver or netdev (single-module/insmod safe)
   - does not call SSR

 Single module (ipa-driver.ko), so the new ipa_dp.c symbol needs only a
 prototype in ipa_i.h, no EXPORT_SYMBOL.

 Generated: 2026-06-09
================================================================

